 S.A. from the Costafreda Family, La Caixa and other minority shareholders.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:5c7fef030a04a1e936632e930c9f4263","date":"2005-10-11","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Bezeq","portco_name":"Bezeq","target_website":"bezeq.co.il","investor":"Apax Partners","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":["Saban Capital Group","Arkin Communications"],"seller":"Israeli Government","round":null,"stake_pct":30.0,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Apax Partners Funds, Saban Capital Group and Arkin Communications (Apax Saban Arkin Group) completes acquisition of controlling interest in leading Israeli telecom company Bezeq","summary":"The Apax Saban Arkin Group closed its purchase of a controlling 30% stake in Israeli telecom operator Bezeq from the state for NIS 4.246 billion, with an option on a further 10.7%.","source_name":"Apax","source_url":"https://www.apax.com/news-views/apax-partners-funds-saban-capital-group-and-arkin-communications-apax-saban-arkin-group-completes-acquisition-of-controlling-interest-in-leading-israeli-telecom-company-bezeq/","evidence":"The group has acquired 30% of Bezeq's shares for 4.246 billion NIS ($923 million) and an option to purchase an additional 10.7% of the shares within the next four years.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:5fff857ffab57225f7e6f81b970b28b0","date":"2005-11-07","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Spectrum Laboratory Network","portco_name":"Spectrum Laboratory Network","target_website":null,"investor":"Apax Partners","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Apax Partners, L.P. to acquire majority ownership interest in Spectrum Laboratory Network","summary":"Apax funds agreed to acquire a majority interest in North Carolina clinical laboratory provider Spectrum Laboratory Network, with founder Moses Cone Health System keeping a significant stake; no price was disclosed.","source_name":"Apax","source_url":"https://www.apax.com/news-views/apax-partners-lp-to-acquire-majority-ownership-interest-in-spectrum-laboratory-network/","evidence":"Spectrum Laboratory Network, a leading regional provider of clinical laboratory and disease screening services, and Apax Partners, L.P., one of the world's leading private equity investment groups, today announced that funds advised by Apax Partners will acquire a majority ownership interest in Spectrum.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:1f9f373b8945a5db6bba7d03cd9ed965","date":"2005-12-12","date_text":null,"kind":"company_exit","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Kabel Deutschland","portco_name":"Kabel Deutschland","target_website":null,"investor":"Providence Equity Partners","sponsor_is_investor":false,"sponsor_role":"seller","co_investors":[],"seller":"Apax Partners and Goldman Sachs Capital Partners","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Providence Equity Partners to take sole ownership of Kabel Deutschland","summary":"Providence Equity Partners agreed to buy out Apax's and Goldman Sachs Capital Partners' stakes in German cable operator Kabel Deutschland, which the three had carved out of Deutsche Telekom in 2003; no price was disclosed.","source_name":"Apax","source_url":"https://www.apax.com/news-views/providence-equity-partners-to-take-sole-ownership-of-kabel-deutschland/","evidence":"Providence Equity Partners will acquire the entire shareholdings of Apax Partners and Goldman Sachs Capital Partners and with about 95% ownership become the sole shareholder of Kabel Deutschland alongside management.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:1125fc0932deddcc4019f10f6ade7690","date":"2005-12-20","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Somerfield Plc","portco_name":"Somerfield Plc","target_website":null,"investor":"Violet Acquisitions Limited","sponsor_is_investor":false,"sponsor_role":null,"co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Somerfield Plc completion of acquisition by Violet Acquisitions Limited","summary":"Violet Acquisitions Limited completed its scheme acquisition of UK supermarket group Somerfield, paying 197p a share in cash or loan notes; the release gives no total.","source_name":"Apax","source_url":"https://www.apax.com/news-views/somerfield-plc-completion-of-acquisition-by-violet-acquisitions-limited/","evidence":"The Scheme has now become effective and the entire issued share capital of Somerfield is owned by Violet Acquisitions Limited. Somerfield Shareholders on the register at the Scheme Record Time, being 6.00 p.m. on 20 December 2005, will receive either 197 pence in cash for each Scheme Share or Loan Notes under the Loan Note Alternative in accordance with valid elections made by them.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:526eebe31fd809f16d99a265bc2201b5","date":"2005-12-23","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Tommy Hilfiger Corporation","portco_name":"Tommy Hilfiger Corporation","target_website":"tommy.com","investor":"Apax Partners","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":1600000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"enterprise_value","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Tommy Hilfiger Corporation announces agreement to be acquired by Funds advised by Apax Partners for $16.80 per share or approximately $1.6 billion","summary":"Apax funds agreed to take NYSE-listed Tommy Hilfiger private at $16.80 a share in cash, a transaction value of about $1.6 billion.","source_name":"Apax","source_url":"https://www.apax.com/news-views/tommy-hilfiger-corporation-announces-agreement-to-be-acquired-by-funds-advised-by-apax-partners-for-1680-per-share-or-approximately-16-billion/","evidence":"Tommy Hilfiger Corporation and Apax Partners, a leading global private equity firm, announced today a definitive agreement under which Funds advised by Apax Partners will acquire Tommy Hilfiger Corporation in a merger at a price of $16.80 per share in cash, representing a transaction value of approximately $1.6 billion.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:f53019c86f86b4979275f3ddf3aecb01","date":"2006-01-20","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"TDC A/S","portco_name":"TDC","target_website":null,"investor":"Nordic Telephone Company ApS","sponsor_is_investor":false,"sponsor_role":null,"co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":null,"valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Nordic Telephone Company's tender offer for all TDC Shares","summary":"Nordic Telephone Company's DKK382-a-share tender offer for Danish telecom operator TDC drew acceptances for about 88.2% of the shares; the release gives no total.","source_name":"Apax","source_url":"https://www.apax.com/news-views/nordic-telephone-companys-tender-offer-for-all-tdc-shares/","evidence":"NTC is pleased to announce that a preliminary count of delivered acceptances shows that, as of approximately 00.01h, Central European Time on 20 January 2006, NTC owned or had received valid acceptances in respect of approximately 88.2% of the share capital and votes of TDC A/S (\"TDC\"), including TDC Shares represented by tendered TDC ADSs and TDC ADSs tendered through guaranteed delivery procedures. The offer price in the Tender Offer was DKK382 per TDC Share and the U.S. dollar equivalent of DKK191 per TDC ADS in cash, without interest and subject to adjustment as described in NTC's Offer Document dated 2 December 2005 relating to the Tender Offer (the \"Offer Document\").","verified":null},{"key":"pr:6e9075d034ba98195153aea8af68aab4","date":"2006-02-01","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"CONTECH Construction Products Inc.","portco_name":"CONTECH Construction Products","target_website":null,"investor":"Apax Partners Worldwide","sponsor_is_investor":true,"sponsor_role":"investor","co_investors":[],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":1000000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"enterprise_value","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Apax Partners completes acquisition of CONTECH; CONTECH realigns for improved customer service and growth","summary":"Apax funds completed the purchase of a majority interest in civil engineering products maker CONTECH at a total enterprise valuation the release puts at more than $1 billion.","source_name":"Apax","source_url":"https://www.apax.com/news-views/apax-partners-completes-acquisition-of-contech-contech-realigns-for-improved-customer-service-and-growth/","evidence":"CONTECH Construction Products Inc., a leading civil engineering site solutions products and services company, and funds advised by Apax Partners Worldwide, one of the world's leading private equity investment groups, today announced that Apax Partners Worldwide have completed their acquisition of a majority ownership interest in CONTECH. The transaction had a total enterprise valuation of more than $1 billion.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:4ac572aef18d4e0ab71ff66c2ba28ff8","date":"2006-03-17","date_text":null,"kind":"company_exit","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Hansen Transmissions International NV","portco_name":"Hansen Transmissions","target_website":null,"investor":"Suzlon Energy Limited","sponsor_is_investor":false,"sponsor_role":"seller","co_investors":[],"seller":"Allianz Capital Partners GMBH and its affiliates and funds advised by Apax Partners","round":null,"stake_pct":null,"amount":465000000.0,"currency":"EUR","amount_basis":"enterprise_value","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Suzlon Energy signs definitive agreement for strategic acquisition of Hansen Transmissions","summary":"Suzlon Energy agreed to buy Belgian gearbox maker Hansen Transmissions from Allianz Capital Partners and Apax funds for a €465 million enterprise value in cash.","source_name":"Apax","source_url":"https://www.apax.com/news-views/suzlon-energy-signs-definitive-agreement-for-strategic-acquisition-of-hansen-transmissions/","evidence":"Suzlon Energy Limited (\"Suzlon\") announced today that its subsidiary, AE - Rotor Holding BV based in Netherlands, has entered into definitive agreements to acquire Hansen Transmissions International NV (\"Hansen\"), based in Belgium, one of the largest wind energy and industrial gearbox manufacturers in the world, for EUR 465 million (USD 565 million) enterprise value, in an all cash transaction. The transaction is subject to merger control approval and on completion will result in Suzlon acquiring shares of \"Eve Holding\", the holding company of Hansen from private equity firms Allianz Capital Partners GMBH and its affiliates and funds advised by Apax Partners Worldwide LLP.","verified":true}]}$pf$::jsonb;
  n_companies int;
  n_deals int;
begin
  select id into gp from public.companies
   where category = 'GP' and name = 'Apax'
   order by (source = 'master_directory') desc nulls last, created_at
   limit 1;
  if gp is null then raise exception 'sponsor % is not in the directory', 'Apax'; end if;

  insert into public.portfolio_companies as pc (external_key, gp_company_id, name, domain, description, sector, hq, status, invested_year, exit_year, fund_name,
      source, source_url, deal_value, deal_currency, deal_value_basis, stake_pct, co_investors, deal_source_url, researched_at)
  select gp::text || ':' || (c->>'slug'), gp, c->>'name', c->>'domain', c->>'description', c->>'sector', c->>'hq', c->>'status',
         (c->>'invested_year')::int, (c->>'exit_year')::int, c->>'fund_name', 'web_research', c->>'source_url',
         (c->>'deal_value')::numeric, c->>'deal_currency', c->>'deal_value_basis', (c->>'stake_pct')::numeric,
         coalesce(array(select jsonb_array_elements_text(c->'co_investors')), '{}'), c->>'deal_source_url', now()
    from jsonb_array_elements(doc->'companies') c
  on conflict (external_key) do update set
    name = case when pc.source = 'manual' then pc.name else excluded.name end,
    domain = coalesce(pc.domain, excluded.domain),
    description = case when pc.source = 'manual' then coalesce(pc.description, excluded.description) else coalesce(excluded.description, pc.description) end,
    sector = case when pc.source = 'manual' then coalesce(pc.sector, excluded.sector) else coalesce(excluded.sector, pc.sector) end,
    hq = case when pc.source = 'manual' then coalesce(pc.hq, excluded.hq) else coalesce(excluded.hq, pc.hq) end,
    status = coalesce(excluded.status, pc.status),
    invested_year = coalesce(excluded.invested_year, pc.invested_year),
    exit_year = coalesce(excluded.exit_year, pc.exit_year),
    fund_name = coalesce(excluded.fund_name, pc.fund_name),
    source_url = case when pc.source = 'manual' then coalesce(pc.source_url, excluded.source_url) else excluded.source_url end,
    deal_value = coalesce(excluded.deal_value, pc.deal_value),
    deal_currency = case when excluded.deal_value is not null then excluded.deal_currency else pc.deal_currency end,
    deal_value_basis = case when excluded.deal_value is not null then excluded.deal_value_basis else pc.deal_value_basis end,
    stake_pct = coalesce(excluded.stake_pct, pc.stake_pct),
    co_investors = case when cardinality(excluded.co_investors) > 0 then excluded.co_investors else pc.co_investors end,
    deal_source_url = coalesce(excluded.deal_source_url, pc.deal_source_url),
    researched_at = now();
  get diagnostics n_companies = row_count;

  insert into public.deals as d (external_key, date, date_text, kind, asset_class, target, target_kind, target_key, target_website, investor, investor_company_id,
      co_investors, seller, round, stake_pct, amount, currency, amount_basis, valuation, valuation_currency, headline, summary, source_name, source_url,
      evidence, verified, source)
  select x->>'key', (x->>'date')::date, x->>'date_text', x->>'kind', x->>'asset_class', x->>'target', 'company',
         public.borrower_key(coalesce(x->>'portco_name', x->>'target')), x->>'target_website', x->>'investor',
         case when (x->>'sponsor_is_investor')::boolean then gp else (select m.company_id from ingest.match_firm(x->>'investor', array['GP']) m) end,
         coalesce(array(select jsonb_array_elements_text(x->'co_investors')), '{}'), x->>'seller', x->>'round', (x->>'stake_pct')::numeric,
         (x->>'amount')::numeric, x->>'currency', x->>'amount_basis', (x->>'valuation')::numeric, x->>'valuation_currency',
         x->>'headline', x->>'summary', x->>'source_name', x->>'source_url', x->>'evidence', (x->>'verified')::boolean, 'web_research'
    from jsonb_array_elements(doc->'deals') x
  on conflict (external_key) do update set
    date = excluded.date, date_text = excluded.date_text, kind = excluded.kind, target = excluded.target, target_key = excluded.target_key,
    target_website = coalesce(excluded.target_website, d.target_website), investor = excluded.investor,
    investor_company_id = coalesce(excluded.investor_company_id, d.investor_company_id),
    co_investors = (select coalesce(array_agg(distinct v), '{}') from unnest(d.co_investors || excluded.co_investors) v),
    seller = coalesce(excluded.seller, d.seller), round = coalesce(excluded.round, d.round), stake_pct = coalesce(excluded.stake_pct, d.stake_pct),
    amount = excluded.amount, currency = excluded.currency, amount_basis = excluded.amount_basis,
    valuation = excluded.valuation, valuation_currency = excluded.valuation_currency, headline = excluded.headline,
    summary = coalesce(excluded.summary, d.summary), source_name = excluded.source_name, source_url = excluded.source_url,
    evidence = excluded.evidence, verified = coalesce(excluded.verified, d.verified);
  get diagnostics n_deals = row_count;

  update public.companies set portfolio_note = 'apax.com Partnerships list via its Umbraco search endpoint /umbraco/apax/SearchSurface/partnerships?page=1..15 (179 cards) with each /partnerships/<slug>/ page for year, sector, country, status and website; plus all 399 /news-views/ press releases (SearchSurface/news?page=1..43) for acquisitions not on the list, and the Apax Partners Wikipedia article', portfolio_researched_at = now() where id = gp;
  insert into ingest.log (what, detail) values ('load_portfolio', jsonb_build_object('sponsor', 'Apax', 'companies', n_companies, 'deals', n_deals));
end $pfdo$;
